# 6. COPY
# Copy files from your host/build context into the image
COPY index.html /app/index.html

COPY . .       means: Copy everything from the current build context into the current destination directory in the image.  Copy everything in the build context

COPY config/ /app/config/     Copy one file 

COPY app.jar /app/app.jar

COPY target/*.jar $APP_HOME/app.jar
target/
└── myproject-1.0.jar
Then this: COPY target/*.jar $APP_HOME/app.jar
renames/copies that JAR inside the Docker image as: /app/app.jar

So:
myproject-1.0.jar  →  app.jar

app.jar is not a special Docker command or special Java file. It's simply the name we choose for the application JAR inside the container.
Copies a file from your project/build context into the image.

So remember:

COPY *.jar /app/
       ↑
       JAR must be directly in build context

whereas:

COPY target/*.jar /app/
      ↑
      look inside target/

