# 8. EXPOSE
# Document which port the application uses
EXPOSE 8080

EXPOSE is mainly used to tell/document which port the application inside the container listens on.
Suppose your Java application runs on:
Container
└── Java application
    └── listening on 8080

You write: EXPOSE 8080

But this does NOT make port 8080 accessible from your host.
To access it from your host, you need:
docker run -p 8080:8080 myapp
